Photo: RNZ / Diego Opatowski
Ray Smith appeared before parliament's law and order select committee today as part of the department's annual review.
Mr Smith was questioned by Labour, the Green Party and New Zealand First over Auckland's Mt Eden Prison and whether the department failed in its oversight of the prison.
Labour's Phil Goff said private operator Serco, which was running the prison at the time, did a "disastrous job" and asked Mr Smith who took responsibility for that.
